From 14d7a102e2b3e8c86d2b0d35c4085e6185761858 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mawaid Build <mawaid-build@local>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 01:32:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add multi-clinic support: one shared service can now run
 several clinics

Adds an internal Add Clinic page (/admin/clinics) where entering a new
clinic's details and WhatsApp credentials and clicking Save brings that
clinic online immediately in this same running app -- no new Railway
service, no git branch, no redeploy.

How it works:
- Each clinic gets its own row in a new local clinics database
  (data/control.db), holding its WhatsApp access token/phone number
  ID/WABA ID, its hours/address/services/dentists/offers, and its
  subscription plan.
- Each clinic still gets its own separate database file and its own
  separate clinic_config.yaml under data/clinics/<slug>/, so clinics are
  fully isolated on disk from one another, the same way separate Railway
  services used to isolate them.
- Each clinic gets its own MCP tool subprocess (same mechanism as before,
  just one per clinic instead of one for the whole app), launched with
  that clinic's own credentials/config/database path in its environment.
- The shared /webhook endpoint reads which WhatsApp number each incoming
  message arrived on and routes it to that clinic's own worker.
- Saving the Add Clinic form also calls Meta's subscribed_apps endpoint
  to point that clinic's WABA at this same app -- the one Meta-side call
  needed per clinic, done automatically instead of by hand.
- The clinic that was already live before this change is carried over
  automatically on first startup (from its existing environment
  variables and config/clinic_config.yaml), pointing at its EXISTING
  database file, so no patient/appointment history is lost or needs
  migrating.

New required Railway variable: ADMIN_PASSWORD (protects /admin/clinics
via a login prompt; username defaults to "admin", override with
ADMIN_USERNAME if wanted).

New Python dependencies: pyyaml (already an indirect dependency, now
explicit), python-multipart (needed for the Add Clinic form's file
upload).
